(4368800, 629938, 36499, '<td valign="top">great concept youve got here but i think this wouldve done better If you had used a womans hands with the man standing there...at least for me. the hand on the torso looks like its got a few too many fingers. try putting a bit of light on the right side of the photo..doesnt have to be as strong bu you want a bit of light over there. also try either moving the one light back a bit or using a sheet to diffuse the light a bit as you have a bit of a hot spot there(could be my monitor tho). your focus and comp and POV are perfect for a shot like this. good luck. this is just my unprofessional opinion.. just trying to help.<br/>~~Cher~~</td>', 'great concept youve got here but i think this wouldve done better If you had used a womans hands with the man standing there...at least for me. the hand on the torso looks like its got a few too many fingers. try putting a bit of light on the right side of the photo..doesnt have to be as strong bu you want a bit of light over there. also try either moving the one light back a bit or using a sheet to diffuse the light a bit as you have a bit of a hot spot there(could be my monitor tho). your focus and comp and POV are perfect for a shot like this. good luck. this is just my unprofessional opinion.. just trying to help.~~Cher~~', '2008-01-07 06:05:03.000000', NULL, 1),
