(4369242, 629756, 7786, '<td valign="top">It took me a while to find the time lapse in this one. Hope other voters wont be as slow or slower than me. Well done.</td>', 'It took me a while to find the time lapse in this one. Hope other voters wont be as slow or slower than me. Well done.', '2008-01-07 09:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(4369243, 629694, 88385, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but it isn''t executed effectively. I''m seeing a thin line of white pixels where the images overlap - my guess is the erase tool didn''t get as close as it needed to with several layers... <br/> <br/>Good idea, though.</td>', 'I like the idea, but it isn''t executed effectively. I''m seeing a thin line of white pixels where the images overlap - my guess is the erase tool didn''t get as close as it needed to with several layers...  Good idea, though.', '2008-01-07 09:59:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4369244, 629751, 88385, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure if the grain was added at at the right time in the editing sequence, for such a field of depth. With the aged texture in the face of the clock, I wonder if the grain was even necessary? It seems sort as though my browser has only loaded the right side of the image, so my eyes keep drifting up to the upper left hand corner.<br/> <br/>I like the idea, though.</td>', 'I''m not sure if the grain was added at at the right time in the editing sequence, for such a field of depth. With the aged texture in the face of the clock, I wonder if the grain was even necessary? It seems sort as though my browser has only loaded the right side of the image, so my eyes keep drifting up to the upper left hand corner. I like the idea, though.', '2008-01-07 09:59:23.000000', NULL, 1),
