(4371231, 628429, 61818, '<td valign="top">Can''t say this works for me even setting aside the triptych thing.</td>', 'Can''t say this works for me even setting aside the triptych thing.', '2008-01-07 19:08:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371240, 629851, 61818, '<td valign="top">Dislike the big gap between the lower left ball and the rest, it makes the image look disjointed and ruins the sense of movement.  Halos around the balls aren''t so hot either.  Setting that aside (and putting my hand over the lower left ball), I like this shot a lot.</td>', 'Dislike the big gap between the lower left ball and the rest, it makes the image look disjointed and ruins the sense of movement.  Halos around the balls aren''t so hot either.  Setting that aside (and putting my hand over the lower left ball), I like this shot a lot.', '2008-01-07 19:09:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371242, 629883, 55838, '<td valign="top">Perfectly entertaining!  Very well done.  Back to bump you up to 9 for bringing a huge smile to my face.  (Not as huge as your models'' but pretty big none-the -less!).  : )  Such a fun shot!</td>', 'Perfectly entertaining!  Very well done.  Back to bump you up to 9 for bringing a huge smile to my face.  (Not as huge as your models'' but pretty big none-the -less!).  : )  Such a fun shot!', '2008-01-07 19:09:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371250, 629494, 61818, '<td valign="top">Makes a nice abstract but really doesn''t convey any sense of passing time.  I don''t think the wilting flower thing is a good one for ''time lapse'' as far as photography goes, though I always enjoy watching videos along these lines.</td>', 'Makes a nice abstract but really doesn''t convey any sense of passing time.  I don''t think the wilting flower thing is a good one for ''time lapse'' as far as photography goes, though I always enjoy watching videos along these lines.', '2008-01-07 19:10:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371255, 629744, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing this won''t pass the natural motion test, but the lighting is pretty harsh here and the shot lacks excitement.</td>', 'I''m guessing this won''t pass the natural motion test, but the lighting is pretty harsh here and the shot lacks excitement.', '2008-01-07 19:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371262, 628895, 50695, '<td valign="top">karmabreeze: this is definitely natural motion. It is the triggering of a massive karmic wheel.<br/> <br/>scalvert: the finger is relaxed on the trigger. Therefore the motion is not due to Newtonian''s Law of Equal and Opposite Motion, but rather a simple flexing of the wrist muscle. It is not natural motion.<br/> <br/>ursula: This is a staged shot with motion planned by the photographer. Therefore it is not natural.<br/> <br/>sher: But people are natural. Thought is natural. If this person thought to jerk his wrist upward, then that is as natural as a leaf falling.<br/> <br/>scalvert: don''t be ridiculous. It''s obvious that premeditated acts of will are not natural.<br/> <br/>muckpond: he''s taking somebody out. That''s totally natural!<br/> <br/>scalvert: but it''s staged.<br/> <br/>muckpond: all your shots are staged.<br/> <br/>scalvert: yes but never in a challenge that demanded natural motion.<br/> <br/>muckpond: what do you mean? your shot in THIS CHALLENGE is staged.<br/> <br/>scalvert: yes, but it is a staged occurence of natural motion. I have certifications from three independent physicists.</td>', 'karmabreeze: this is definitely natural motion. It is the triggering of a massive karmic wheel. scalvert: the finger is relaxed on the trigger. Therefore the motion is not due to Newtonian''s Law of Equal and Opposite Motion, but rather a simple flexing of the wrist muscle. It is not natural motion. ursula: This is a staged shot with motion planned by the photographer. Therefore it is not natural. sher: But people are natural. Thought is natural. If this person thought to jerk his wrist upward, then that is as natural as a leaf falling. scalvert: don''t be ridiculous. It''s obvious that premeditated acts of will are not natural. muckpond: he''s taking somebody out. That''s totally natural! scalvert: but it''s staged. muckpond: all your shots are staged. scalvert: yes but never in a challenge that demanded natural motion. muckpond: what do you mean? your shot in THIS CHALLENGE is staged. scalvert: yes, but it is a staged occurence of natural motion. I have certifications from three independent physicists.', '2008-01-07 19:12:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371263, 629322, 61818, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  Think it might have worked better with a slower shutter so the ping pong balls were leaving longer trails.  That would really kick up the sens of motion and passing time.  Here it almost looks like the kid shot off five ping pong balls in a row and you got the shot when they were all in the air.</td>', 'Nice idea.  Think it might have worked better with a slower shutter so the ping pong balls were leaving longer trails.  That would really kick up the sens of motion and passing time.  Here it almost looks like the kid shot off five ping pong balls in a row and you got the shot when they were all in the air.', '2008-01-07 19:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371266, 629686, 61818, '<td valign="top">Nice time of day to shoot at, got some good light.</td>', 'Nice time of day to shoot at, got some good light.', '2008-01-07 19:12:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371274, 629486, 61818, '<td valign="top">Don''t think this one plays by the (nearly impossible to comprehend) rules.  Has sort of a modern abstract feel to it.</td>', 'Don''t think this one plays by the (nearly impossible to comprehend) rules.  Has sort of a modern abstract feel to it.', '2008-01-07 19:13:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371277, 629523, 61818, '<td valign="top">Good concept, good captures - wrong place to shoot it.  The blown out sky and pea-soup shade of green in the bottom half really take the photo down a notch or three.</td>', 'Good concept, good captures - wrong place to shoot it.  The blown out sky and pea-soup shade of green in the bottom half really take the photo down a notch or three.', '2008-01-07 19:14:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371282, 629739, 61818, '<td valign="top">Don''t suppose you get to tell the deer to wait while you find the best angle to shoot from, but it''s pretty hard to see the deer here due to all the foreground obstruction.</td>', 'Don''t suppose you get to tell the deer to wait while you find the best angle to shoot from, but it''s pretty hard to see the deer here due to all the foreground obstruction.', '2008-01-07 19:15:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371290, 629757, 61818, '<td valign="top">Nice b/w conversion and I like the ominous, industrial feel of the shot.  Would look nicer if the planes weren''t overlapped.</td>', 'Nice b/w conversion and I like the ominous, industrial feel of the shot.  Would look nicer if the planes weren''t overlapped.', '2008-01-07 19:15:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371295, 629945, 50695, '<td valign="top">GeneralE: this is more complex than the single swing of a golfer. <br/> <br/>ursula: yes, but it''s still one lovely line of motion.<br/> <br/>GeneralE: but it intersects itself, cuts itself in two.<br/> <br/>ursula: but by the time it gets to itself, it''s not there anymore.<br/> <br/>GeneralE: clearly you know nothing about topology.<br/> <br/>scalvert: the photograph incriminates itself. Clearly there is someone flying this kite. That person is using muscles, will, thought, etc. to effect the flight pattern of the kite. It''s not natural.<br/> <br/>ursula: It''s the wind. The wind is natural. She''s just holding it to create the proper tension to allow the wind to work on it.<br/> <br/>scalvert: but that''s an unnatural method for portraying natural phenomena.<br/> <br/>ursula: so is pohtography.</td>', 'GeneralE: this is more complex than the single swing of a golfer.  ursula: yes, but it''s still one lovely line of motion. GeneralE: but it intersects itself, cuts itself in two. ursula: but by the time it gets to itself, it''s not there anymore. GeneralE: clearly you know nothing about topology. scalvert: the photograph incriminates itself. Clearly there is someone flying this kite. That person is using muscles, will, thought, etc. to effect the flight pattern of the kite. It''s not natural. ursula: It''s the wind. The wind is natural. She''s just holding it to create the proper tension to allow the wind to work on it. scalvert: but that''s an unnatural method for portraying natural phenomena. ursula: so is pohtography.', '2008-01-07 19:16:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371307, 629705, 61818, '<td valign="top">Pretty good shot.  The composition bothers my eye a bit in that everything about the shot is fairly symmetrical except for their placement in the frame which is inexplicably skewed just enough to the left to make the shot unbalanced.</td>', 'Pretty good shot.  The composition bothers my eye a bit in that everything about the shot is fairly symmetrical except for their placement in the frame which is inexplicably skewed just enough to the left to make the shot unbalanced.', '2008-01-07 19:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371310, 629823, 50695, '<td valign="top">GeneralE: this is unnatural. a step is missing.<br/> <br/>muckpond: he''s going out for food. it''s totally natural!<br/> <br/>GeneralE: how do you know that?<br/> <br/>muckpond: I can tell by his expression.<br/> <br/>scalvert: it''s clearly a staged shot. the next thing he''s going to do is turn around and pick up his camera. Not natural.<br/> <br/>sher: it''s natural. It''s raining so you lift an umbrella. What''s more natural than that?</td>', 'GeneralE: this is unnatural. a step is missing. muckpond: he''s going out for food. it''s totally natural! GeneralE: how do you know that? muckpond: I can tell by his expression. scalvert: it''s clearly a staged shot. the next thing he''s going to do is turn around and pick up his camera. Not natural. sher: it''s natural. It''s raining so you lift an umbrella. What''s more natural than that?', '2008-01-07 19:18:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371314, 629425, 61818, '<td valign="top">Would work better if all the fish were as well captured as the leftmost specimen, but I know fish are tough to shoot in their dim little tanks.</td>', 'Would work better if all the fish were as well captured as the leftmost specimen, but I know fish are tough to shoot in their dim little tanks.', '2008-01-07 19:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371323, 629583, 61818, '<td valign="top">Surprised I haven''t seen more of these golfer shots.  Good job on the golfer.  The nauseatingly over-saturated colors in the shot really make it look amateurish though.</td>', 'Surprised I haven''t seen more of these golfer shots.  Good job on the golfer.  The nauseatingly over-saturated colors in the shot really make it look amateurish though.', '2008-01-07 19:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371329, 629694, 61818, '<td valign="top">Have to say it''s another shot that suffers from too much of a good thing.  Rather than conveying a sense of motion over time, this just looks like a crowd of guys in red jackets jostling each other around.</td>', 'Have to say it''s another shot that suffers from too much of a good thing.  Rather than conveying a sense of motion over time, this just looks like a crowd of guys in red jackets jostling each other around.', '2008-01-07 19:20:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371331, 629744, 50695, '<td valign="top">GeneralE: this is one of those polykiwi shots. unnatural.<br/> <br/>sher: but the man is moving in a circle.<br/> <br/>GeneralE: but then he walks through the wall and faces himself. Not natural.<br/> <br/>ursula: no, he looks in *first* and *then* he decides to go in through the door. Finally, he circles around to the window, where he thinks about he was just outside looking in. Memories are natural.<br/> <br/>scalvert: thought processes are not natural. Only Newtonian physics is natural. This is so unnatural it isn''t funny.<br/> <br/>ursula: I think it''s kinda funny. Look at his expression in the window. And look at that cute dog!</td>', 'GeneralE: this is one of those polykiwi shots. unnatural. sher: but the man is moving in a circle. GeneralE: but then he walks through the wall and faces himself. Not natural. ursula: no, he looks in *first* and *then* he decides to go in through the door. Finally, he circles around to the window, where he thinks about he was just outside looking in. Memories are natural. scalvert: thought processes are not natural. Only Newtonian physics is natural. This is so unnatural it isn''t funny. ursula: I think it''s kinda funny. Look at his expression in the window. And look at that cute dog!', '2008-01-07 19:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371334, 629339, 61818, '<td valign="top">Heh, this is cool in that it looks like some sort of genetically mutated lion with three faces.  Other than that I''m not sure what to make of it.</td>', 'Heh, this is cool in that it looks like some sort of genetically mutated lion with three faces.  Other than that I''m not sure what to make of it.', '2008-01-07 19:21:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371341, 629577, 61818, '<td valign="top">Nice capture and you put it together well.  Little underexposed and could use a bit more contrast imo.</td>', 'Nice capture and you put it together well.  Little underexposed and could use a bit more contrast imo.', '2008-01-07 19:21:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371351, 629885, 61818, '<td valign="top">Too much bird to get a good sense of what is happening.  A shame really because the two on the left are really well captured with great detail and the perfect amount of motion blur on the wings, but the right side just becomes a soup of brown and white.</td>', 'Too much bird to get a good sense of what is happening.  A shame really because the two on the left are really well captured with great detail and the perfect amount of motion blur on the wings, but the right side just becomes a soup of brown and white.', '2008-01-07 19:22:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371360, 628727, 61818, '<td valign="top">Have to say there just isn''t much going on here to enjoy.  While you appear to have put the technique to use, I have to believe that the ends are more important than the means.</td>', 'Have to say there just isn''t much going on here to enjoy.  While you appear to have put the technique to use, I have to believe that the ends are more important than the means.', '2008-01-07 19:23:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371366, 628985, 61818, '<td valign="top">Too much foreground biker and it obscures a good deal of the motion going on in the background.  The bits of him driving down the road are the most interesting parts of the shot and it''s unfortunately hard to see back there.</td>', 'Too much foreground biker and it obscures a good deal of the motion going on in the background.  The bits of him driving down the road are the most interesting parts of the shot and it''s unfortunately hard to see back there.', '2008-01-07 19:24:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371371, 629557, 61818, '<td valign="top">Cool, really cool.  Wish the biker was a bit brighter so he didn''t fade into the background, but otherwise a fine shot.</td>', 'Cool, really cool.  Wish the biker was a bit brighter so he didn''t fade into the background, but otherwise a fine shot.', '2008-01-07 19:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371373, 629226, 50695, '<td valign="top">sher: so shots of people walking are not natural but shots of a gull walking is natural?<br/> <br/>scalvert: no. nothing''s natural (except physics).<br/> <br/>frisca: gulls have no Will. they are natural. everything they do is driven by instinct.<br/> <br/>ursula: how do you know that gulls aren''t thinking. have you ever looked on in the eye?<br/> <br/>frisca: it''s theologically impossible.<br/> <br/>scalvert: ag! no theology! physics says no. Physics is going to give me another ribbon.<br/> <br/>GeneralE: walking requires physics.<br/> <br/>scalvert: yes, but not one single smooth motion of physics.<br/> <br/>ursula: I don''t recall seeing "single" or "smooth" in the rules.<br/> <br/>scalvert: it''s implied by natural.<br/> <br/>ursula: that''s funny. I''ve never seen nature be singular or smooth.<br/> <br/>scalvert: what are you? a Quantum physicist?</td>', 'sher: so shots of people walking are not natural but shots of a gull walking is natural? scalvert: no. nothing''s natural (except physics). frisca: gulls have no Will. they are natural. everything they do is driven by instinct. ursula: how do you know that gulls aren''t thinking. have you ever looked on in the eye? frisca: it''s theologically impossible. scalvert: ag! no theology! physics says no. Physics is going to give me another ribbon. GeneralE: walking requires physics. scalvert: yes, but not one single smooth motion of physics. ursula: I don''t recall seeing "single" or "smooth" in the rules. scalvert: it''s implied by natural. ursula: that''s funny. I''ve never seen nature be singular or smooth. scalvert: what are you? a Quantum physicist?', '2008-01-07 19:25:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371374, 629863, 55838, '<td valign="top">Very nice detail and a great catch.  Back to bump you up to 9.</td>', 'Very nice detail and a great catch.  Back to bump you up to 9.', '2008-01-07 19:25:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371376, 629823, 61818, '<td valign="top">Excellent in all regards.  I''m half way through voting and this is my pick of the litter so far.</td>', 'Excellent in all regards.  I''m half way through voting and this is my pick of the litter so far.', '2008-01-07 19:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4371380, 629441, 61818, '<td valign="top">Now here''s a ski shot I can get into.  Great choice of captures to combine while leaving enough space between the skiers to convey a sense of motion and not clutter up the scene.  Well done.</td>', 'Now here''s a ski shot I can get into.  Great choice of captures to combine while leaving enough space between the skiers to convey a sense of motion and not clutter up the scene.  Well done.', '2008-01-07 19:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
