(4382657, 629850, 50695, '<td valign="top">GeneralE: that''s not a natural chord progression. I think he''s bending notes.<br/> <br/>ursula: the Blues is natural.<br/> <br/>scalvert: but is it physics?<br/> <br/>ursula: it''s physical.</td>', 'GeneralE: that''s not a natural chord progression. I think he''s bending notes. ursula: the Blues is natural. scalvert: but is it physics? ursula: it''s physical.', '2008-01-10 19:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382669, 629754, 50695, '<td valign="top">GeneralE: looks like a single motion to me.<br/> <br/>Manic: I think he''s trying to fool us into thinking there are three dogs.<br/> <br/>GeneralE: some of us are more easily fooled than others.<br/> <br/>Manic: What are you trying to say?</td>', 'GeneralE: looks like a single motion to me. Manic: I think he''s trying to fool us into thinking there are three dogs. GeneralE: some of us are more easily fooled than others. Manic: What are you trying to say?', '2008-01-10 19:53:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382672, 629287, 22384, '<td valign="top">Great concept. I would like to have seen the angle changed so that I as the view could see the actual catch. The placement of your focal point seems off and I thing would the "rule of thirds" would also improve this shot. Again, though, great concept!</td>', 'Great concept. I would like to have seen the angle changed so that I as the view could see the actual catch. The placement of your focal point seems off and I thing would the "rule of thirds" would also improve this shot. Again, though, great concept!', '2008-01-10 19:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382682, 629557, 50695, '<td valign="top">muckpond: hella jump! let''s give him the blue ribbon!<br/> <br/>scalvert: we''re only discussing validation here.<br/> <br/>L2: that''s right, the Site Council hasn''t awarded a ribbon since DrAchoo payed us off for that ladybug shot.</td>', 'muckpond: hella jump! let''s give him the blue ribbon! scalvert: we''re only discussing validation here. L2: that''s right, the Site Council hasn''t awarded a ribbon since DrAchoo payed us off for that ladybug shot.', '2008-01-10 19:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382758, 629705, 22384, '<td valign="top">Cute picture and the movement of the leaves add so much to this image. Well done!8</td>', 'Cute picture and the movement of the leaves add so much to this image. Well done!8', '2008-01-10 20:09:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382810, 629823, 67237, '<td valign="top">hmmm... i think i''ve seen that rainbow umbrella before in other challenge :-)<br/>very good pov, <br/>shutter speed was not fast enough to freeze action in captures 3 and 4..there is some motion blur there, specially in number 3...but it may have been on purpose.<br/>processing looks good<br/>nice texture on floor and bg.<br/>border ads to the composition<br/>a solid 9 from me</td>', 'hmmm... i think i''ve seen that rainbow umbrella before in other challenge :-)very good pov, shutter speed was not fast enough to freeze action in captures 3 and 4..there is some motion blur there, specially in number 3...but it may have been on purpose.processing looks goodnice texture on floor and bg.border ads to the compositiona solid 9 from me', '2008-01-10 20:17:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382832, 629339, 67237, '<td valign="top">how could this be assumed as a single natural sequence? it may and it may not..the only way to check is by seeing the sequence of originals.<br/>I am glad you have not been DQd as others just because of the doubt (apparently you have not been asked for vaslidation either). Weird double standards here. Good Luck!!</td>', 'how could this be assumed as a single natural sequence? it may and it may not..the only way to check is by seeing the sequence of originals.I am glad you have not been DQd as others just because of the doubt (apparently you have not been asked for vaslidation either). Weird double standards here. Good Luck!!', '2008-01-10 20:21:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382848, 629705, 67237, '<td valign="top">very nice and creative idea for the challenge, but , as many others, there is no way to verify this complies with the rules without seeing the sequence of originals, since this is not necesarily a natural sequence of a single motion.<br/>I will give you the benefit of the doubt, and considering the technicals, particularly the efective use of dof, a 9 from me</td>', 'very nice and creative idea for the challenge, but , as many others, there is no way to verify this complies with the rules without seeing the sequence of originals, since this is not necesarily a natural sequence of a single motion.I will give you the benefit of the doubt, and considering the technicals, particularly the efective use of dof, a 9 from me', '2008-01-10 20:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4382856, 629863, 67237, '<td valign="top">wow...look at that texture on the water surface!<br/>nice, clean composition, with good technicals.<br/>assuming it fits the rules (no way to confirm it without seeing the original sequence) this is another solid 9</td>', 'wow...look at that texture on the water surface!nice, clean composition, with good technicals.assuming it fits the rules (no way to confirm it without seeing the original sequence) this is another solid 9', '2008-01-10 20:26:44.000000', NULL, 1),
