(4404849, 629878, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like the shot.  I like how he is entering the frame on one side, and he just partially shows, then is exiting the frame on the other, and still just partially shows.  Your space between the bikes is good.<br/> <br/>Technically, I like the color of the rider against the "bland" sky.  Yea, a better sky would have made it more dramatic, but some things we can''t control.  Converting it to bw would help the sky, but then the rider would be lost in the details of the trees.  I don''t like the "texture" that the tonemapping gave the grass.  I know that is a personal thing, and others really like it, but to me it looks almost grainy -- like it is out of focus or was underexposed and had to be brought up so much it made it edgy.  Just my opinion though.  I think the vignetting may be a bit much.  Perhaps if it were more subtle.  <br/> <br/>Overall, a very effective shot.  <br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I like the shot.  I like how he is entering the frame on one side, and he just partially shows, then is exiting the frame on the other, and still just partially shows.  Your space between the bikes is good. Technically, I like the color of the rider against the "bland" sky.  Yea, a better sky would have made it more dramatic, but some things we can''t control.  Converting it to bw would help the sky, but then the rider would be lost in the details of the trees.  I don''t like the "texture" that the tonemapping gave the grass.  I know that is a personal thing, and others really like it, but to me it looks almost grainy -- like it is out of focus or was underexposed and had to be brought up so much it made it edgy.  Just my opinion though.  I think the vignetting may be a bit much.  Perhaps if it were more subtle.   Overall, a very effective shot.   Karma', '2008-01-19 15:06:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4405419, 629557, 89062, '<td valign="top">I am so new to this having only had a camera since Christmas but this is awesome. What a crystal clear and FUN picture. I have no idea about the work involved in such a shot, but if I could ever do this I''d be amazed. Great job.</td>', 'I am so new to this having only had a camera since Christmas but this is awesome. What a crystal clear and FUN picture. I have no idea about the work involved in such a shot, but if I could ever do this I''d be amazed. Great job.', '2008-01-19 20:25:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4406618, 628989, 55956, '<td valign="top">Critique club greeting.<br/> <br/>The final result of this photo is 6.14, during the voting my vote was 6 hence I am in the average.<br/> <br/>why 6 and not a more high score? the photo securely meet the challenge but nearly in scholastic mode. As you write in your comment, there isn''t a great image quality and the angle is too much high. There aren''t particulary solutions to these problem, perhaps cropping the image near the first man could do a better impression.</td>', 'Critique club greeting. The final result of this photo is 6.14, during the voting my vote was 6 hence I am in the average. why 6 and not a more high score? the photo securely meet the challenge but nearly in scholastic mode. As you write in your comment, there isn''t a great image quality and the angle is too much high. There aren''t particulary solutions to these problem, perhaps cropping the image near the first man could do a better impression.', '2008-01-20 13:53:18.000000', NULL, 0),
